// Development workspace.
//
// The raster backends, the window backend, the opt-in GPU tier and the Arrow
// adapter are separate modules so that importing figure's core keeps a
// stdlib-only dependency graph. During development they are built together from
// this workspace; released builds resolve the core through the require
// directive in each nested module's go.mod.
//
// The workspace says go 1.27.1 because backend/stilus does: its font library
// requires it (docs/adr/0094). That raises nothing for any other module — each
// one's own go.mod is still what a user's build reads, and the core and the gg
// modules still declare 1.25. CI checks that declaration on Go 1.25 with a
// workspace of its own that leaves backend/stilus out.
go 1.27.1

use (
	.
	./arrow/v18
	./backend/gg
	./backend/gg/gpu
	./backend/stilus
	./backend/window
)
